1
00:00:00,685 --> 00:00:04,480
What happens when a vision-language-action policy learns from demonstrations,

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,830
but fails during physical execution?

3
00:00:08,085 --> 00:00:13,410
This is EmbodiedOps, a failure-driven evaluation and verification system for robot learning.

4
00:00:16,085 --> 00:00:20,965
I connected SmolVLA to RoboCasa and MuJoCo, with three camera observations,

5
00:00:20,965 --> 00:00:26,005
robot proprioception, action-chunk execution, and physical contact diagnostics.

6
00:00:28,085 --> 00:00:33,205
I then tested several post-training strategies. The key finding was that lower imitation loss

7
00:00:33,205 --> 00:00:36,775
did not consistently translate into better robot performance.

8
00:00:40,085 --> 00:00:45,860
Here is one example. In the archived seed sixty-four evaluation, the frozen policy closes the

9
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:49,890
refrigerator, while the recontact fine-tuned policy fails.

10
00:01:02,085 --> 00:01:06,845
Instead of automatically accepting the new checkpoint, EmbodiedOps uses NVIDIA Nemotron through

11
00:01:06,845 --> 00:01:08,620
Nebius Token Factory.

12
00:01:18,085 --> 00:01:22,195
Nemotron calls real tools to inspect the model, compare trajectories,

13
00:01:22,195 --> 00:01:26,565
examine contact evidence, and request independent physical verification.

14
00:01:45,085 --> 00:01:50,790
The new evaluation also rejects the candidate. Importantly, the frozen model does not reproduce

15
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:55,620
its earlier success, revealing another limitation in closed-loop reproducibility.

16
00:01:56,085 --> 00:02:01,695
The final decision is made by deterministic acceptance checks, not by the language model's narrative.

17
00:02:01,695 --> 00:02:07,115
In fact, the model makes a mistake in its final explanation. The structured results contradict

18
00:02:07,115 --> 00:02:10,310
it; the independent rejection remains authoritative.

19
00:02:11,285 --> 00:02:16,655
EmbodiedOps does not claim a successful autonomous repair. It demonstrates an auditable agentic

20
00:02:16,655 --> 00:02:22,495
workflow connecting VLA post-training, physical robot evaluation, evidence-driven tool use,

21
00:02:22,495 --> 00:02:24,425
and independent verification.
